hello my name is kurt busch  and i'm co-founder and ceo of sentient  we started sentient to build a new type  of processor to make  ai truly pervasive along with  specialized silicon  we developed an artificial intelligence  training pipeline  as well as a data platform that has  allowed us to ship over 10 million units  that are being deployed today in things  as small as earbuds  to as large as automobiles  [Music]  when we started sentient in 2017 we had  this idea for a processor architecture  that could bring  200 times the efficiency 20 times the  performance  and at half the cost of existing edge  processors  now the device can run multiple types of  applications but we were looking for  a single application to go to market  first that would have a significant  societal impact one day i saw my  youngest son  talk to his ipad and i said what are you  doing  he says i'm texting my friends and you  know my response  was was pretty clear is that said vinnie  you can't read  and you certainly can't type so what are  you doing because well i just talked to  it  that's when the light bulb went off and  i called up my co-founders and i said  let's make  voice the interface of the future  and after thinking about user interfaces  for a while we saw that the first  interface to the computer was the  keyboard  and with ms-dos that shipped at about  150 million units a year  the next was the mouse and with windows  that ships at about 500 million units a  year  and in each step it gets easier the next  interface which we all carry with us  is the touch screen and that's in the  smartphone and that's about a billion  five units a year  so we think that voice will be the next  generation interface  and the volumes could be 3x or even more  than what we see today  in the smartphone our processors are  currently used in applications from  event detection such as glass  breaking or fall detection wake words  command words speaker id  the devices can support multiple  applications running in parallel an  extremely small  power footprint so you could have a wake  word plus command word plus speaker id  say is it curt is it not curt and these  types of applications  can be deployed to enable ai and voice  interfaces without an always-on cloud  connection and coming soon we'll be  bringing a full speech interface  that can make speech truly a first-class  way of interacting with just about any  device  speech is not just a natural interface  for people but it requires no  training whatsoever when we first saw  that voice  was the next generation user interface  it was really enabled  by amazon and the amazon echo  if amazon hadn't come out with the echo  and put alexa devices  in everyone's home they really wouldn't  think of voice as the next generation  interface  so today according to unesco  approximately three quarters of a  billion people  are uncomfortable with reading and  writing and by adding a speech interface  to a low-cost cell phone  we can bring all of those people into  the digital age  and they can benefit from all of the  economic and educational advantages  that come with a digital connection  from earbuds to automobiles sentient is  making voice the next generation user  interface  [Music]  you
 

